  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_031: multimodal, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieves 0.678 acc, only modestly above the RNA-only baseline (config_005: 0.650). Image-only resnet50 is very weak (0.208), raising uncertainty about whether the image modality has untapped signal or is near its ceiling. Config_037 changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l (keeping scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fixed), directly isolating the effect of image encoder quality in the multimodal setting. If imagenet_vit_l yields a meaningful gain, it signals the image branch has more capacity to exploit and justifies further multimodal exploration; if it does not, it confirms the image contribution is inherently limited and the budget is better spent refining RNA-side choices. This single-variable comparison from the current best is the most efficient way to reduce uncertainty about the image modality's ceiling under the limited budget."
}

